msgid "Introduction"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A proxy acts as an intermediary between an application and external services."
"\n"
"Instead of connecting directly to a remote host, the application sends "
"requests through a proxy server.\n"
"The proxy server then forwards the requests to the destination."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In Java applications, proxies are commonly required in environments where "
"direct outbound network access is restricted.\n"
"This is typical in corporate networks.\n"
"This is also common in cloud environments with strict security rules.\n"
"This is often required in production systems that require traffic inspection "
"and auditing."
msgstr ""

msgid "Proxies are commonly used to:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Control and restrict outbound network access"
msgstr ""

msgid "Enforce security and network policies"
msgstr ""

msgid "Provide authentication for external connections"
msgstr ""

msgid "Monitor and log outgoing traffic"
msgstr ""

msgid "Proxy configuration"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Many Java applications rely on JVM system properties or client-specific "
"configuration to enable proxy support.\n"
"This approach can lead to duplicated configuration.\n"
"This approach can also lead to inconsistent behavior across clients."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus provides a centralized way to configure proxies using the Proxy "
"Registry.\n"
"All proxy configuration is defined under the `quarkus.proxy` configuration "
"root."
msgstr ""

