msgid "Using credentials"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Proxy authentication can be configured directly using the `username` and "
"`password` properties."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Credentials can be externalized using environment variables.\n"
"Credentials can also be externalized using any other supported Quarkus "
"configuration source."
msgstr ""

msgid "Providing credentials via a Credentials Provider"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Instead of defining credentials directly in configuration, you can integrate "
"with a Quarkus Credentials Provider.\n"
"This allows credentials to be retrieved securely from external systems.\n"
"Examples include vaults or secret managers."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This feature relies on the xref:credentials-provider.adoc[Credentials "
"Provider] capability."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To configure a credentials provider for proxy authentication, use the "
"following properties:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The Proxy Registry automatically retrieves the credentials.\n"
"The credentials are applied to the proxy configuration."
msgstr ""

msgid "How credentials are applied"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When a proxy is configured with a Credentials Provider, the Proxy Registry "
"automatically retrieves the credentials at startup.\n"
"The retrieved credentials are applied to the proxy configuration."
msgstr ""

msgid "The behavior is as follows:"
msgstr ""

msgid "If `username` and `password` are explicitly configured, they are used."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Otherwise, if a Credentials Provider is configured, the credentials are "
"retrieved from the provider."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If no credentials are configured, the proxy is used without authentication."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If only one of `username` or `password` is defined, the application fails at "
"startup.\n"
"The application also fails if the credentials cannot be retrieved from the "
"provider.\n"
"In both cases, a configuration error is reported."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This ensures that proxy configuration is validated early.\n"
"This validation is consistent across all clients and extensions."
msgstr ""

